  "body": "Part of #894. Found while working #985 (external threads on a boss).\n\n**What happens.** A Thread operation's feature list is filled only by Detect holes / Detect bosses, which reads every round upright wall of the source model. For bosses that includes a round base the boss stands on (a round wall is a boss too), so #985 added a per-row Remove button on the Thread page to trim the list. There is no way to add ONE feature by clicking it.\n\n**What is owed.** On the Thread page's Geometry tab, a pick through the one pick rule (#692): clicking a cylindrical outer face or its circular edge adds that boss (centre, major radius, top, shoulder) to an external thread's list; clicking a bore wall or its rim adds that hole to an internal one. A pick of the wrong kind (a hole for an external thread) is refused by name. The pick lands as one undoable `EditOperationParams`; an MCP tool (or a param on an existing one) does the same headlessly. `drilling::recognize_bosses` / `recognize` already give the feature for a wall; the pick only has to choose which.\n\n**Done means:** a boss and a hole can each be added to a Thread operation by one viewport pick and by MCP, undo removes it, a wrong-kind pick is refused by name; pinned by an app test and a UI frame test.\n",
